DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__AATT__nnaammee() creates a DW_AT_name attribute descriptor
     and attaches it to the debugging information entry referenced by argument
     _d_i_e.  The created attribute will have DWARF form DW_FORM_strp.

     Argument _d_i_e should reference a debugging information entry allocated us‐
     ing dwarf_new_die(3).

     Argument _n_a_m_e should point to a NUL-terminated string which will become
     the value of the created attribute.

     If argument _e_r_r is not NULL, it will be used to store error information
     in case of an error.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     On success, function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__AATT__nnaammee() returns the created attribute
     descriptor.  In case of an error, function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__AATT__nnaammee() returns
     DW_DLV_BADADDR and sets the argument _e_r_r.

EERRRROORRSS
     Function ddwwaarrff__aadddd__AATT__nnaammee() can fail with:

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]  One of the arguments _d_i_e or _n_a_m_e was NULL.

     [DW_DLE_MEMORY]    An out of memory condition was encountered during the
                        execution of this function.

